          "description": {
            "comment": "The Red-legged Seriema (Cariama cristata) is a predatory terrestial bird in the Cariamidae family. It is found in the grasslands of Brazil, south of the Amazon to Uruguay and northern Argentina. The Red-legged Seriema has a song described to sound like a cross between a bark of a young dog and a clucking of turkeys (description from B10K Avian Phylgenomics Project http://gigadb.org/dataset/101018). This sample was collected by Mads Bertelsen from a female that lived at the Copenhagen Zoo in Denmark, originally in Holland, and was procured by Tom Gilbert to be used to generate a chromosome level reference assembly as part of the G10K-VGP and B10K Projects.",
